Date: 2026-06-25 19:00:18 +0000

Detect and clean up blob heads stranded on the wrong partition

The real problem was not that array tasks 10-15 failed to run (the flocks
confirm all 16 ran) but that partition 001 still physically holds the a-f
head directories. Until commit 7dc01fb (2026-05-13), BLOBS_HEAD_TO_PARTITION
mapped heads 10-15 -> 001, so every a-f blob was backed up there. After the
mapping changed, new writes correctly go to 002, but `s5cmd cp` never deletes,
so the stale a-f copies remain stranded in 001. (Earlier churn on heads 7 and
9 may likewise have left stale copies in 002.)

- verify-blobs: now flags a head present on a partition it is not assigned to
  (MISPLACED), in addition to missing writes. This is the check that actually
  catches the a-f-in-001 condition.
- Add `s3backup dandi cleanup-misplaced-blobs [--apply]`: removes misplaced
  head sub-directories from the wrong partition. Safe by default - dry run
  unless --apply, and a directory is deleted only once the correct partition
  holds a byte-for-byte complete copy, so no data is lost; incomplete copies
  are reported and skipped.
- README: document the cleanup workflow.

